{"Start Here":{"B1":"Cleaning Business System - Start Here","B2":"Clients, jobs, invoices, payments, expenses and a monthly profit report in one file. Type each thing once - the rest fills in for you.","B4":"HOW THE COLORS WORK","B5":"Teal column headers = you type here (many cells have dropdown lists).","B6":"Dark gray headers and light gray cells = automatic. Please don't type over them.","B7":"Yellow cells on the Settings tab = your business details and price list.","B9":"SET UP IN 5 STEPS","B10":"1. Settings: enter your business name, sales tax rate (0% if you don't charge tax), payment terms and P&L year.","B11":"2. Settings: list your services and your standard price for each one (room for 15).","B12":"3. Clients: add each client once - name, address, usual service, and a custom price if they have one.","B13":"4. Jobs: add a row for every job. Pick the date, pick the client, and set Status to Completed when it's done.","B14":"5. Invoices: completed jobs show up as invoices. When a client pays, log it in the Payments Log on the same tab.","B15":"    The Monthly P&L tab then adds up revenue, expenses, profit and cash collected for each month.","B17":"YOUR FIRST JOB IN 60 SECONDS","B18":"1. Clients tab: in the first empty row type a name (for example Jane Test) and an address, then pick Standard Clean under Usual Service.","B19":"2. Jobs tab: in the first empty row type today's date (Ctrl + ; in Excel), pick Jane Test under Client,","B20":"    and pick Completed under Status.","B21":"3. Look right on the same row: address, price, tax, total and invoice number are already filled in.","B22":"4. Invoices tab: Jane Test's invoice is at the end of the list with its due date and status.","B23":"5. Monthly P&L tab: this month's revenue went up by that job (if the P&L year on Settings is this year).","B24":"    Done testing? Clear the cells you typed on Clients and Jobs and everything goes back.","B26":"HOW TO CLEAR THE SAMPLE DATA (all formulas stay in place)","B27":"Select each range below and press the Delete key. Use Delete only - not 'Delete Row' or 'Delete Sheet'.","B28":"    Clients tab:   A5:H204","B29":"    Jobs tab:   A5:H504","B30":"    Expenses tab:   A5:F504","B31":"    Invoices tab (Payments Log):   M5:P1004","B32":"Quick way: click the Name Box (left of the formula bar), type the range, press Enter, then press Delete.","B33":"Then replace the sample business details and prices on the Settings tab with your own.","B35":"GOOD TO KNOW","B36":"Dates: type real dates like 7/14/2026. The file refuses text that isn't a date, so due dates and days overdue always work.","B37":"Leave Service blank on a job to use the client's usual service and custom price. Pick a different service to charge its standard price.","B38":"Rate Override on a job beats every other price. Qty is visits or hours (blank = 1). Extras adds a flat amount, e.g. inside oven.","B39":"Only Completed jobs become invoices and count as revenue. Scheduled and Cancelled jobs are kept for your records.","B40":"Add new rows at the bottom of each list. Don't sort the Jobs tab or delete job rows - invoice numbers come from the job's line.","B41":"    To drop a job, set its Status to Cancelled instead.","B42":"Client names must be unique (the file will warn you). Avoid * and ? in client names.","B43":"Room for 200 clients, 500 jobs, 500 expenses and 1,000 payments."},"Settings":{"A1":"Settings","A2":"Yellow cells are yours to change. Everything else in the file reads from here.","A4":"Setting","B4":"Your value","D4":"Service type","E4":"Standard rate ($)","F4":"Rate basis / notes","H4":"Expense categories","J4":"Payment methods","A5":"Business name","B5":"Sparkle & Shine Cleaning Co.","D5":"Standard Clean","E5":120.0,"F5":"per visit","H5":"Cleaning Supplies","J5":"Cash","A6":"Owner / contact name","B6":"Your Name","D6":"Deep Clean","E6":220.0,"F6":"per visit","H6":"Equipment","J6":"Check","A7":"Phone","B7":"(555) 010-2040","D7":"Move-In / Move-Out","E7":320.0,"F7":"pe